@HostAddress = http://localhost:5000/api/v1
@adminToken = {{loginAdmin.response.body.data.accessToken}}
@refreshToken = {{loginAdmin.response.body.data.refreshToken}}

### ==========================================================================
### 1. AUTHENTICATION & SECURITY (JWT + Refresh Tokens + RBAC)
### ==========================================================================

### 1.1 Login as Default Admin (Seeded on Startup)
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{HostAddress}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@studententerprise.com",
  "password": "EnterpriseAdmin@2026!"
}

###

### 1.2 Register a Teacher (Assigns "Teacher" Role)
POST {{HostAddress}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "prof.joshi@enterprise.edu",
  "password": "TeacherPassword@2026!",
  "fullName": "Prof. Arvind Joshi",
  "role": "Teacher"
}

###

### 1.3 Register a Student User (Default Role)
POST {{HostAddress}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "sachin.tendulkar@enterprise.edu",
  "password": "StudentPassword@2026!",
  "fullName": "Sachin Tendulkar",
  "role": "Student"
}

###

### 1.4 Login as Teacher
# @name loginTeacher
POST {{HostAddress}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "prof.joshi@enterprise.edu",
  "password": "TeacherPassword@2026!"
}

###

### 1.5 Token Rotation: Refresh Token using Expired/Active Access Token + Refresh Token
POST {{HostAddress}}/auth/refresh-token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accessToken": "{{adminToken}}",
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

###

### 1.6 Revoke Refresh Token
POST {{HostAddress}}/auth/revoke-token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

###

### 1.7 Get Current Authenticated Profile
GET {{HostAddress}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 1.8 Get All Enterprise Roles (Admin Only)
GET {{HostAddress}}/auth/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

### ==========================================================================
### 2. CQRS & REPOSITORY CRUD (Students)
### ==========================================================================

### 2.1 Get Paged Students (Page 1, Size 5, Sort by Name Ascending)
GET {{HostAddress}}/students?pageNumber=1&pageSize=5&sortBy=Name&isAscending=true
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 2.2 Search & Filter Students (Search "Deshmukh", Course "Computer Science")
GET {{HostAddress}}/students?searchTerm=Deshmukh&course=Computer%20Science
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 2.3 Get Student Statistics by Course
GET {{HostAddress}}/students/statistics
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 2.4 Get Student by ID
GET {{HostAddress}}/students/1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 2.5 Create Student (Admin / Teacher Only)
POST {{HostAddress}}/students
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Neha Kulkarni",
  "email": "neha.kulkarni@enterprise.edu",
  "age": 21,
  "course": "Artificial Intelligence",
  "phoneNumber": "+91 9988776655"
}

###

### 2.6 Update Student (Admin / Teacher Only)
PUT {{HostAddress}}/students/1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Amit Deshmukh (Lead Developer)",
  "email": "amit.deshmukh@enterprise.edu",
  "age": 22,
  "course": "Cloud Computing",
  "phoneNumber": "+91 9876543210",
  "isActive": true
}

###

### 2.7 Delete Student (Admin Only)
DELETE {{HostAddress}}/students/3
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

### ==========================================================================
### 3. EDGE / NEGATIVE CASES TESTING
### ==========================================================================

### 3.1 [Negative] 400 Bad Request - FluentValidation Failure (Invalid Email & Negative Age)
POST {{HostAddress}}/students
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "A",
  "email": "invalid-email-string",
  "age": -5,
  "course": ""
}

###

### 3.2 [Negative] 401 Unauthorized - Missing Token
GET {{HostAddress}}/students/1
Accept: application/json

###

### 3.3 [Negative] 404 Not Found - Non-Existent Record
GET {{HostAddress}}/students/999999
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 3.4 [Negative] 409 Conflict - Duplicate Email on Create
POST {{HostAddress}}/students
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Duplicate Student",
  "email": "amit.deshmukh@enterprise.edu",
  "age": 22,
  "course": "Computer Science"
}
